  "verbalization": "Norwogonin-8-O-glucuronide appears to exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways that ultimately target the FaDu cell line. The evidence suggests that the compound acts as a target for several enzymes or proteins, including DNA polymerase iota, which is subsequently targeted by (3R,3S)-3-O-Methylviolanone and another related compound. These intermediates are themselves targets of FaDu, indicating a cascade of molecular interactions that may contribute to the observed effects. The presence of multiple targets, each with a documented relationship to FaDu, supports a potential mechanism involving the modulation of DNA polymerase activity, which could influence cellular processes critical to the disease state. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions, with the compound potentially influencing cellular functions through different routes, all converging on the FaDu cell line. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
